  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental balances: beginning_cash/ending_cash are the Total Governmental Funds fund balances (61,753 and 133,930, p4), which roll forward with receipts, disbursements and transfers (p4); the actual cash is 66,536 plus investments 53,353 and due from other governments 16,180 less bank overdraft 2,139 (p3). Transfers in/out 40,000 (Keno to Auditorium & Park) are printed at total level (out is within Other Governmental Funds). Business-type: Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p6); no single total printed: receipts = total operating revenues 231,272 + interest and investment revenue 5,341; disbursements = total operating expenses 204,377 + interest expense 21,288; 939,456 + 236,613 - 225,665 = 950,404. Proprietary cash flow statement is modified cash basis so proprietary is null. Balance sheet = Statement of Net Position, Primary Government 2025 Total column (p1); bank overdraft classified as other liabilities. Detail: budget schedules for all funds (budget_final = 'Original and Final' column); budgetary-basis actuals for Water and Sewer exclude depreciation and include debt service and capital outlay (differ from p6). Keno Fund schedule prints no revenue or expenditure totals so none recorded. Misc revenue 19,319 on p4 not broken down in the statement; fund schedules show General 2,540, Auditorium 5,708, Keno 9,069, Cemetery 1,628, Fire 374. Read pages 1-16 of 16 (v7 re-trim added p8, the proprietary cash flow reconciliation continuation: nothing new to record; page numbers remapped). Water and Sewer budget-schedule Debt service lines split into principal and interest using the proprietary cash flow statement (p7); Sewer interest taken as 28,391 less 9,927 = 18,464 (p7 prints 18,465, rounding); combined debt service budgets (32,823 Water, 28,392 Sewer) not split, so budget_final is null on those lines."
